From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] survive: enable global scene calibration by default

WiVRn was overriding libsurvive's default with --globalscenesolver 0.
This prevents global scene calibration in fresh installations without saved
base station poses, even though buttons and device configs still arrive.
Use libsurvive's default of 1; keep SURVIVE_GLOBALSCENESOLVER as an override.

---
diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c b/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/survive/survive_driver.c
@@ -1275,7 +1275,7 @@
 
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_LOG_OPTION(survive_log, "SURVIVE_LOG", U_LOGGING_WARN)
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_OPTION(survive_lh_gen, "SURVIVE_LH_GEN", "0")
-DEBUG_GET_ONCE_OPTION(survive_global_scene_solver, "SURVIVE_GLOBALSCENESOLVER", "0")
+DEBUG_GET_ONCE_OPTION(survive_global_scene_solver, "SURVIVE_GLOBALSCENESOLVER", "1")
 
 static void
 add_device(struct survive_system *ss, const struct SurviveSimpleConfigEvent *e)
